{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"940a94b9-7954-4d97-a263-16d3f4c2d745","content":"This confirms the mechanism directly. Now I have the answer.\n\n## Answer\n\nThere's no \"fall back to English strings for missing pages\" mechanism in VitePress — locales are just separate routed directories (`docs/da/**`), and if a file (or generated dir) doesn't exist under a locale prefix, that route simply 404s. This repo doesn't build content-level fallback; it relies on keeping every locale's directory in parity (`docs/scripts/check-locale-parity.ts`).\n\nThe actual bug you hit is that **`vpr docs:dev` never generates locale API docs at all**:\n\n- [docs/package.json](docs/package.json)'s `docs:dev` script runs `docs:api:en` (English-only TypeDoc build), not `docs:api:locales`. So `docs/da/api/` (and every other locale's `api/`) is never created locally.\n- `docs:api:locales` (invoked by `docs:build:all`/`docs:dev:all`) is the script that actually clones the English TypeDoc output into each locale folder (e.g. `docs/da/api/`) and machine-translates it.\n- The production build (`docs:build`) works around this differently: it sets `DOCS_ROOT_LOCALE_ONLY=1`, which adds `${locale}/api/**` to `srcExclude` in [docs/.vitepress/config.ts](docs/.vitepress/config.ts#L625) — pruning non-root API routes from the site entirely rather than trying to serve them.\n\nSo under plain `docs:dev`, visiting `/da/api/` 404s because that directory genuinely doesn't exist on disk yet. To see localized API docs locally, run `vp run docs:dev:all` instead (or `vp run docs:api:locales` once, then `vp run docs:dev`).","toolRequests":[]},"id":"1c3ded56-c870-4e74-9b0f-518304eb3e8a","timestamp":"2026-09-03T21:56:36.396Z","parentId":"761d0d8c-bc7b-45d2-b330-814d1232f990"}
